<?jelly escape-by-default='true'?>
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core" xmlns:l="/lib/layout" xmlns:f="/lib/form">
    <div class="jenkins-alert jenkins-alert-warning">
        <l:isAdmin>
            <form method="post" action="${rootURL}/${it.url}/disable" name="${it.id}">
                <f:submit name="no" value="Dismiss"/>
            </form>
        </l:isAdmin>
        Pipeline DORA Metrics keeps its database at <code>${it.databasePath}</code>, on a network filesystem
        (<code>${it.fileSystem}</code>). SQLite is not reliable on network storage, and slow writes there can delay
        builds. Move it to a persistent directory on local disk: start Jenkins with
        <code>-D${it.directoryProperty}=/a/directory/on/local/disk</code> after copying <code>metrics.db</code> there
        while Jenkins is stopped, or, while Jenkins is stopped, move the <code>pipeline-dora-metrics</code> folder to
        local disk and link it back.
    </div>
</j:jelly>
